## Examples (MOST IMPORTANT)
- examples/memories/agent_memory_example.py - Example showing an agent with longterm memory usage, saving/loading memory, and interaction.
- examples/toolkits/human_toolkit.py - Example showing an agent using human interaction tools (ask_human_via_console, send_message_to_user).
- examples/agents/single_agent.py - Basic single agent example with prompt usage.
- examples/rag/single_agent_with_hybrid_rag.py - Example of a single agent using retrieval augmented generation (RAG) pattern.

## Implementation
- camel/agents/chat_agent.py - Base ChatAgent class (implied from imports, core for agent creation).
- camel/memories/chat_history_memory.py (implied from example) - Memory implementation used for longterm memory.
- camel/toolkits/human_toolkit.py - Toolkit implementation for human interaction tools.

## Configs and Types
- camel/configs/chat_gpt_config.py (implied from usage in human_toolkit example) - Model configuration.
- camel/types/enums.py - Enums for ModelType, ModelPlatformType, RoleType, etc.

## Summary
To create an agent with longterm memory and human interaction tools, you can combine the pattern from `examples/memories/agent_memory_example.py` (for memory) and `examples/toolkits/human_toolkit.py` (for human tools). Use `ChatAgent` with a memory instance and human toolkit tools. Then write a test query similar to the examples.

I can help generate the script `task-script/single_agent/9_longterm_memory_single_agent.py` based on these patterns if you want.
